--- What it means for you, plainly ---

Calling the hosted API, or installing and using the picker component, is
consuming a Produced Work. It imposes nothing on your application. Your app does
not become ODbL.

Redistributing the DATABASE does trigger share-alike. If you take our dumps, or
derive a database from them, and publicly use the result, you must offer that
derived database under ODbL as well.

That distinction is ODbL's, not ours, and it is why the two licences are stated
separately rather than as one.

